   "messageId": "message:provider:codex:native-item:msg_0ce4d5e3f8f059e3016aed13ff705487d2a859086243c9d05c",
   "text": "# Renaming rooms in the Kestrel directory\n\n## 1. Keep room identity separate from its name\n\nKestrel is a fictional directory of shared work rooms. Each room has a room key and a display name. These serve different purposes: the key identifies the room, while the display name is the human-readable label people see.\n\nKestrel assigns a key when a room is created. That key never changes and is never reused for another room. Room owners can change the display name. A rename therefore changes what people see while preserving the room\u2019s identity.\n\nThis distinction matters when building links. Saved room links identify their destination by key. When someone opens a saved link, Kestrel looks up that key and displays the room\u2019s current name. The link can continue to reach the same room even though the label has changed.\n\nA link built from a display name can stop finding the room after a rename because the name it uses has changed. Use the room key to identify the destination and the display name to label it.\n\nIn the storage schema, these concepts appear as `room_ref`, the key column, and `title_text`, the display-name column. Read those column names with their separate roles in mind.\n\n## 2. Verify both the destination and the displayed name\n\nVerify a rename with a room link saved before the change. Opening that link afterward checks whether the earlier link still reaches the room and whether Kestrel shows its new name.\n\nFollow this sequence:\n\n1. **Save a room link before renaming.** Use a link that identifies the room by its key.\n2. **Rename the room.** As the room owner, change its display name.\n3. **Open the saved link.** It should reach the same room and show the new name.\n\nCheck both results. Seeing the new name checks the displayed label; reaching the same room checks the destination. Together, they verify the expected behavior of the saved link across the rename.\n\nKeep the original saved link for this check. A link saved only after the rename does not verify what happens to a link saved beforehand. The before-and-after sequence connects the two parts of the lesson: a room keeps its key, and Kestrel displays its current name.",
